---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';

const flows = [
  {
    num: '01',
    title: 'Discover',
    text: 'Connectors read the target estate where it already lives: Microsoft 365, Azure, Active Directory, AWS, Google Cloud, endpoint and network inventories. Each collector writes evidence, not opinion.',
  },
  {
    num: '02',
    title: 'Consolidate',
    text: 'One canonical view of people, applications, workspaces, sites, licences and information systems. Conflicts between sources are held open and attributed rather than silently resolved.',
  },
  {
    num: '03',
    title: 'Assess',
    text: 'Security posture, compliance obligations, organisational shape and commercial risk, assembled from the same evidence set so that the diligence pack and the integration plan cannot disagree.',
  },
  {
    num: '04',
    title: 'Plan and migrate',
    text: 'Waves, mappings, runbooks and go/no-go gates. Rehearsals run against recorded state before anything touches a production tenant.',
  },
  {
    num: '05',
    title: 'Operate and close',
    text: 'Day-one command, hypercare queues, synergy tracking and the post-close journal. The estate stays legible after the deal team has moved on.',
  },
];

const index = [
  { href: '/platform/', label: 'The platform', meta: 'Product' },
  { href: '/services/', label: 'Deployment and delivery services', meta: 'Services' },
  { href: '/support/', label: 'Support and technical notes', meta: 'Support' },
  { href: '/security/', label: 'Security and compliance posture', meta: 'Trust' },
  { href: '/status/', label: 'Service status', meta: 'Trust' },
  { href: '/billing/', label: 'Billing and licensing', meta: 'Commercial' },
  { href: '/company/', label: 'The company', meta: 'Company' },
  { href: '/contact/', label: 'Contact', meta: 'Company' },
];
---

<Base title={SITE.name} description={SITE.description}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="micro micro--red hero__kicker reveal">Enterprise software · Installed on your infrastructure</p>
      <h1 class="reveal reveal-2">The target's estate, read before you sign.</h1>
      <p class="hero__lede reveal reveal-3">
        ACQI discovers, consolidates and plans an acquisition target's technology estate.
        It is installed in your own environment and operated by your own team. No target
        data is sent to us, and there is no hosted service to connect to.
      </p>
      <div class="hero__actions reveal reveal-4">
        <a class="btn btn--solid" href="/platform/">See the platform</a>
        <a class="linkarrow" href="/preview/">Open the app preview</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="calligram reveal reveal-4" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="calligram__thread" style="top: 34%"></span>
      <span class="calligram__line">Discovery.</span>
      <span class="calligram__line calligram__line--ghost">Consolidation.</span>
      <span class="calligram__line calligram__line--red">A decision you can defend.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">I</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">How it is delivered</h2>
        <p class="micro section__note">A plain statement of the model</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cols cols--sidebar">
        <div>
          <p class="lede mb-0">
            ACQI is enterprise software you install. It runs on hardware you control, inside
            an Azure subscription or data centre you already own.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            This matters at the point of diligence. A target's asset inventory, identity
            topology, licence position and security findings are among the most sensitive
            documents in a transaction. Routing them through a vendor's multi-tenant platform
            creates a disclosure question that has to be answered in the data room, in the
            security questionnaire and often in the sale and purchase agreement.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-0">
            With ACQI that question does not arise. The application, its database, its
            evidence store and its logs all sit inside your boundary. We supply the installer,
            the licence and the engineering support. You supply the environment and the
            operators.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <dl class="defs mt-3">
        <div>
          <dt>Delivery</dt>
          <dd>Windows desktop application plus a service tier, installed by your team from a signed package. An air-gapped installation is supported.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Data residency</dt>
          <dd>Target data remains in your environment. We do not receive inventories, credentials, documents or findings.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Identity</dt>
          <dd>The application authenticates against your directory. Role assignment stays with your administrators.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Updates</dt>
          <dd>Versioned releases, applied on a schedule you set. No silent background upgrades.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Telemetry</dt>
          <dd>Off by default. If you turn it on, it carries licence counts and error signatures, never estate content.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Exit</dt>
          <dd>Your database and evidence store are documented and exportable. There is no lock-in mechanism in the product.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">II</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">The work it covers</h2>
        <p class="micro section__note">Five stages, one evidence set</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cols cols--3">
        {flows.map((flow) => (
          <article class="card">
            <p class="micro micro--red mb-1">{flow.num}</p>
            <h3>{flow.title}</h3>
            <p>{flow.text}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>

      <p class="mt-3 mb-0">
        <a class="linkarrow" href="/platform/">Read the platform detail</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">III</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">What we do not claim</h2>
        <p class="micro section__note">Stated once, kept current</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cols cols--sidebar">
        <p class="lede mb-0">A short list, because the rest of the market does not keep one.</p>
        <div>
          <ul class="stack-list">
            <li>No customer names, logos or quoted customer praise on this site. Design partners are covered by confidentiality, and we will not spend their trust on a logo strip.</li>
            <li>No usage statistics. We have not published adoption numbers because a number without a method behind it is decoration.</li>
            <li>No certification claimed as held. ISO 27001 and SOC 2 are planned, not achieved, and every page that touches the subject says so.</li>
            <li>No hosted service. Nothing about the product is delivered as multi-tenant SaaS.</li>
            <li>No autonomous changes to a production tenant. Migration actions are proposed, reviewed and executed by your operators.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="small mb-0">
            Where a claim depends on a future event, the page says which event and who owns it.
            See <a href="/security/">Security</a> for the current position.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">IV</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">In this site</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="toc">
        {index.map((item) => (
          <li>
            <a href={item.href}>
              <span class="toc__label">{item.label}</span>
              <span class="toc__leader" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="toc__meta">{item.meta}</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="cols cols--2">
          <div>
            <p class="micro micro--red mb-1">Next step</p>
            <h2 class="mb-1">Bring us a live deal and a date.</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
              The useful first conversation is not a demo. It is a scoping call about the target
              estate, the diligence timetable and where the evidence has to land.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p>
              We will tell you plainly whether the product fits, and what a deployment would
              take in your environment. If it does not fit, we will say so and point you at
              what does.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-0">
              <a class="btn btn--solid" href="/contact/">Start a scoping conversation</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
